t should be prefered.\nIf there are tests on maven that should also be prefered.\nThe \"description\" field must explain what the library does in exactly two sentences.\n\nUpdate this file directly:\n- File: /home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/9946-5feb5a16/build/discovered-artifact-metadata/com.sun.xml.ws-httpspi-servlet-4.0.5.json\n- Use only these top-level JSON keys: \"coordinates\", \"repository-url\", \"source-code-url\", \"test-code-url\", \"documentation-url\", \"description\", \"language\", \"not-for-native-image\", \"reason\", and \"replacement\".\n- Do not add \"metadata-version\"; the metadata index version is derived from the coordinate version later.\n- Set \"coordinates\" to \"com.sun.xml.ws:httpspi-servlet:4.0.5\".\n- Set \"repository-url\" to the discovered repository root URL.\n- Set \"source-code-url\", \"test-code-url\", and \"documentation-url\" to the discovered values with \"$version$\" replacing version \"4.0.5\".\n- Set \"description\" to the selected two-sentence explanation.\n- If any of these URLs or the description cannot be found with confidence, set that field value to \"N/A\".\n- Set \"not-for-native-image\", \"reason\", and \"replacement\" only when the artifact is certainly not a Native Image metadata target.\n- Keep the JSON valid and consistently formatted.\nI hit a hard wall here: this session's permission mode is auto-denying every write operation (`Write`, `Edit`) and every network call (`WebFetch`, `WebSearch`, `curl`, `gh api`) without prompting — not just risky ones, all of them. Per my instructions, I'm stopping rather than trying further workarounds (e.g., forcing a write via a different tool or disabling the sandbox), since that would run against the clear intent of the denial.\n\n**What I found (from sibling metadata already in this repo, high confidence on repo URL; pattern-based for the rest):**\n\nTwo sibling artifacts in this same repo — `com.sun.xml.ws:servlet:4.0.5` and `com.sun.xml.ws:rt:4.0.5` — already confirm this library is part of **Eclipse Metro JAX-WS** (`github.com/eclipse-ee4j/metro-jax-ws`) and follows a consistent URL pattern (Maven Central sources jar + javadoc.io). Based on that pattern and my knowledge of the JAX-WS RI module layout, here's the metadata I was about to write:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"coordinates\" : \"com.sun.xml.ws:httpspi-servlet:4.0.5\",\n  \"repository-url\" : \"https://github.com/eclipse-ee4j/metro-jax-ws\",\n  \"source-code-url\" : \"https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/com/sun/xml/ws/httpspi-servlet/$version$/httpspi-servlet-$version$-sources.jar\",\n  \"test-code-url\" : \"https://github.com/eclipse-ee4j/metro-jax-ws/tree/$version$/jaxws-ri\",\n  \"documentation-url\" : \"https://javadoc.io/doc/com.sun.xml.ws/httpspi-servlet/$version$/index.html\",\n  \"description\" : \"This library implements the Jakarta XML Web Services HTTP SPI (jakarta.xml.ws.spi.http) on top of the Servlet API, adapting HttpServletRequest and HttpServletResponse to the HttpContext, HttpExchange, and HttpHandler abstractions used by JAX-WS endpoints. It lets JAX-WS RI (Eclipse Metro) web service endpoints written against the portable HTTP SPI be hosted inside a standard Servlet container instead of the JDK's lightweight built-in HTTP server.\"\n}\n```\n\nNot language-specific (plain Java), and it's a real JVM artifact (not Android/JS/Native-only), so `language` and `not-for-native-image` are correctly absent.\n\n**Caveat:** `test-code-url` falls back to the generic `jaxws-ri` tree root — same conservative choice the `servlet` sibling made — because I couldn't browse the repo to confirm the exact module subdirectory (likely `jaxws-ri/runtime/httpspi-servlet`, but unverified). Everything else is either directly confirmed by sibling files in this repo or a very standard Maven Central/javadoc.io convention.\n\n**How would you like to proceed?** I can write this once you grant Write/Edit permission for this session, or you can paste it into the file yourself.\n\nEXIT_CODE: 0\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1790964514560}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_L16ZNByarU8m2lrBjUrhVyKf|fc_052048e484730eb7016abff322502c87d1a28e2591b16fa7fa", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "# Instructions when developing tests\n\n## Code Style\n- Tests should throw and assert against standard Java exceptions; do not use `GradleException` in test code.\n- The model may modify `buildArgs` in `build.gradle` only in `graalvmNative` and only to add `--add-opens` or `--add-exports arguments`."}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1790964514560}]}
